STYLE: Replace `Fill(0)` on local variables with `{}` initialization

Replaced code of the form

    Type var;
    var.Fill(0);

and

    Type var;
    var.Fill(ElementType{});

with `Type var{};`

Using Notepad++, Replace in Files, doing:

    Find what: ^( [ ]+)([^ ].* )(\w+);[\r\n]+\1\3\.Fill\(0\.?0?\);
    Find what: ^( [ ]+)([^ ].* )(\w+);[\r\n]+\1\3\.Fill\(.*{}\);
    Replace with: $1$2$3{};
    [v] Match case
    (*) Regular expression

- Following ITK pull request https://github.com/InsightSoftwareConsortium/ITK/pull/4897
commit https://github.com/InsightSoftwareConsortium/ITK/commit/47335501a5a16c6eb42538a829d4b49229284dd6

STYLE: Replace log::get_ostringstream() calls with std::ostringstream{}

Also replaced `auto outputStringStream = log::get_ostringstream()` variable declarations with `std::ostringstream outputStringStream`.

Calling `log::get_ostringstream()` (with takes users specified precision into account) is no longer necessary, because users no longer needs to set the precision of output values.

MS:

-ENH: WriteToFile() is const. I needed to commit a const fix to the ITK for this, so elastix is dependent on the cvs version of the ITK. You can also change the ResampleImageFilter to

  itkGetConstReferenceMacro( DefaultPixelValue, PixelType );

and the BSplineInterpolateImageFunction to

     itkGetConstMacro(SplineOrder, int);

in your local copy.

ENH: Reduce rounding errors "GridSpacingSchedule" GetDefaultParameterMap

For a parameter map returned by `GetDefaultParameterMap`, the values of "GridSpacingSchedule" are meant to approximate consecutive powers of the square root of two, `pow(sqrt(2), n)`, in reverse order.

The original code produced the following values for "GridSpacingSchedule":

    { "2.803221", "1.988100", "1.410000", "1.000000" }

With this commit, it will be:

    { "2.8284271247461903", "2", "1.4142135623730951", "1" }

MS:


-ENH: adding template <class T>
  bool ReadParameter(
    std::vector< T > & parameterValues,
    const std::string & parameterName,
    const unsigned int entry_nr_start,
    const unsigned int entry_nr_end,
    const bool printThisErrorMessage,
    std::string & errorMessage ) const;
which does some checks only once for a set of parameters and returns a complete set instead of just one parameter. We will use it in ReadParameterFile when reading the possibly many transformation parameters.

ENH: Add `RetrieveParameterValue<T>` and RetrieveParameterStringValue

Allows directly initializing a variable by the retrieved parameter value, e.g.:

    const auto parameterValue = configuration.RetrieveParameterStringValue("Default", "ParameterName", 0, false);

Instead of having two statements:

    std::string parameterValue = "Default";
    configuration.ReadParameter(parameterValue, "ParameterName", 0, false);

STYLE: Run clang-format again

Did rerun clang format as follows:

    find . -regex '.*\.\(hxx\|h\|cxx\)' -exec /c/Users/Niels_Dekker/AppData/Roaming/ClangPowerTools/LLVM/LLVM8.0.1/bin/clang-format.exe -style=file -i {} \;

STYLE: Make Base classes abstract by declaring destructors pure virtual

Added comment:

  /** The destructor. Declared "pure virtual" to make this an abstract base class. */

STYLE: Remove local "zero" variables of `DerivativeValueType`

https://github.com/SuperElastix/elastix/blob/0b3bac6dda5d8352a9a082e5f1c3fdbb4812c06e/Common/CostFunctions/itkAdvancedImageToImageMetric.h#L138 says:

    using DerivativeValueType = typename DerivativeType::ValueType;

https://github.com/InsightSoftwareConsortium/ITK/blob/b554b994e0b1cb71a1124f74bcbc4d4d9d6b8905/Modules/Numerics/Optimizers/include/itkSingleValuedCostFunction.h#L59 says:

    using DerivativeType = Array<ParametersValueType>;

https://github.com/InsightSoftwareConsortium/ITK/blob/b554b994e0b1cb71a1124f74bcbc4d4d9d6b8905/Modules/Numerics/Optimizers/include/itkCostFunction.h#L52 says:

    using ParametersValueType = TInternalComputationValueType;

https://github.com/InsightSoftwareConsortium/ITK/blob/b554b994e0b1cb71a1124f74bcbc4d4d9d6b8905/Modules/Numerics/Optimizers/include/itkCostFunction.h#L69 says:

    using CostFunction = CostFunctionTemplate<double>;

So we may conclude that `DerivativeValueType` is indirectly just a typedef for `double`, and it understands the meaning of `0.0` and `{}` initialization.

STYLE: Call DataObject::UpdateSource(), avoid calling GetSource() twice

Replaced the following pattern (13 times):

    if (x->GetSource())
    {
      x->GetSource()->Update();
    }

With `x->UpdateSource();`. DataObject::UpdateSource() was introduced with ITK 5.3.0.

Following ITK pull request https://github.com/InsightSoftwareConsortium/ITK/pull/3603 commit d701a0aa1285c5ca104ada6f56d87b70446dd0fb, 10 September 2022.

